{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unique factorization of polynomials unique factorization of polynomials","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","fileName":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination]] · [[Polynomial Rings and Factorization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Field","Irreducible Polynomial","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unique factorization of polynomials unique factorization of polynomials","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","fileName":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials","heading":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Every nonconstant polynomial over a [[Field]] can be expressed as a product of [[Irreducible Polynomial]]s. Any two such factorizations have the same number of factors after reordering and multiplication of factors by nonzero constants.\n\nThe theorem extends from one-variable to multivariable polynomial rings. It makes irreducible factors the basic multiplicative building blocks of polynomial equations.\n\nThe book derives existence by repeatedly factoring reducible polynomials and uses irreducible divisibility to control uniqueness up to order and associates. This makes irreducible factors the stable data of a polynomial over a field.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Field","Irreducible Polynomial","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unique factorization of polynomials unique factorization of polynomials","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","fileName":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unique Factorization of Polynomials","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Field","Irreducible Polynomial","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}